  "localizations": [
    {
      "type": "appStoreVersionLocalizations",
      "id": "50f7236f-e12e-4d83-a3de-f9f9b12fde52",
      "attributes": {
        "description": "Turn cafe moments and travel snapshots into photos with a nostalgic feel.\nChoose from 8 camera looks, from faded film colors to a 2000s digicam style. Start shooting and saving with 3 free cameras.\n\n3 FREE CAMERAS\n- Plain 70: gently faded colors for everyday snapshots\n- Sunset Fade: warm orange tones for golden-hour moments\n- Y2K Digicam: bright highlights and a coarse, cool-toned 2000s digital look\n\n5 MORE LOOKS, EACH A ONE-TIME PURCHASE\n- Monochrome Film: bold contrast and textured black-and-white grain\n- Pastel Film: bright, soft colors for portraits and cafe moments\n- Night Neon: cool shadows and glowing lights for night scenes\n- Toy Plastic: light leaks and a strong vignette\n- Datestamp 98: a date burned into the corner, like a 90s point-and-shoot\n\nPREVIEW BEFORE YOU BUY\nCompare all 8 looks in the live preview for free. Saving a photo taken with a paid camera requires purchasing that camera.\nEach paid camera is a separate one-time purchase. There is no subscription. Restore bought cameras with Restore Purchases in Settings.\n\nCHOOSE, SHOOT, KEEP\nPick a camera and tap the shutter. The look is applied as you shoot, without adjusting sliders afterward.\nYour shots are also saved to your photo library. Revisit them in the in-app gallery and share through the standard share menu.\n\nRetroSnap is a camera for taking new photos. It does not import or edit existing photos.",
        "locale": "en-US",
        "keywords": "vintage,analog,disposable,monochrome,black,white,pastel,grain,neon,night,toy,light,leak,sepia,90s",
        "marketingUrl": null,
